WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.875
To sum up.

2
00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:03.793
You enabled the internet
profile for the pilot,

3
00:00:03.793 --> 00:00:09.104
built a security profile with one blocked
category and assigned it with Conditional

4
00:00:09.104 --> 00:00:11.797
Access, proved the block,
added the QUIC rule,

5
00:00:11.797 --> 00:00:15.313
checked the inspection issuer,
and read the T L S outcomes.

6
00:00:15.313 --> 00:00:19.732
The evidence an I S S O keeps from
this module: the filtering profile,

7
00:00:19.732 --> 00:00:22.384
policy and Conditional Access exports;

8
00:00:22.384 --> 00:00:26.965
the blocked-category test and the
traffic query; the bypass register;

9
00:00:26.965 --> 00:00:32.028
the certificate and chain, the trust
profile's deployment status, the issuer

10
00:00:32.028 --> 00:00:36.850
check and the failure share; and the
privacy approval and the user notice.

11
00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:42.101
Next is Module 6, rings, rollback and the
evidence package, where the pilot becomes

12
00:00:42.101 --> 00:00:47.090
a migration, and where you roll the whole
test tenant back in the guide's order.
